A||N||4||85ZainoGT||Headlight motor wont stop spinning on the way down||||1||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-14-2001||08:03 PM||||any ideas of what I can do?  it just wont stop spinning, so I had to un-plug it... so, do I just need a new relay or what? thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic2222.jpg"> <BR>NEW pics are coming SOON hopefully... geez!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierobruiser||11-14-2001||09:29 PM||||My 85GT had the same problem at the Williamsburg show. I had to unplug it also.<BR>My problem was that the gear was stripped and needed Rodney's rebuild kit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierobruiser||11-14-2001||09:33 PM||||I note your ID was 85 but your signature is 87. I also just rebuilt my 88 headlights that had a similar problem with Rodney's $8.00 kit. The rollers inside were powdered. Real easy and they work perfectly now. Just make sure when you take them apart you make some registration marks so that you put them back together exactly as they were when you took them apart.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||11-14-2001||09:42 PM||||If you have the 87-88 motors then they need a rebuild with rodneys or another kit. <BR>If you have 84-86 you can turn the gear 180 and clean everything up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||11-14-2001||10:38 PM||||yep, I have one that does that.  I swapped it out with a working one but in the mean time, Just find a bottle cap from like a 20oz, or 2 liter bottle or such.  When the light is down, wedge the bottle cap in place to hold the manual adjust knob.  <P>Its not very good temp fix..  But it will releve you of the need to keep pullin the fuse or the plug.||||reg||1
